            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "are you referring to the `vim.system` below? i think that can be avoided, and it's generally good to avoid when possible. if we're just trying to confirm which CWD is passed to the process, then we can invoke `nvim` itself (`n.nvim_prog`), sth like:\n\n    cmd = { n.nvim_prog, '--clean', 'call writefile(getcwd(), 'Xtest-lsp-cwd')' }\n\nthen the test can assert the contents of `Xtest-lsp-cwd` via `t.retry()` (to avoid timing sensitivity)",
            "commit_id": "cebac5bd860128bafa2f3b30c027329685169cab",
            "created_at": "2026-06-25T23:23:47Z",
